<title>GERMANY: German court declares Ahaus nuclear facility safe.</title>
<headline>German court declares Ahaus nuclear facility safe.</headline>
<dateline>MUENSTER, Germany 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A court in Germany's North Rhine-Westphalia said on Wednesday that an intermediate atomic storage facility was safe and a plea by two citizens against it was unfounded.</p>
<p>The court decided that storage containers at the facility, located near Ahaus near Muenster in North Rhine-Westphalia, were secured against any radiation risk, both in normal operations and in the event of a possible accident.</p>
<p>The containers are used to store fuel elements from the now redundant high-temperature reactor at Hamm-Uetrop.</p>
<p>The German environmental group BUND was critical of the court's decision.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
